==Spanish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|es|osp|prestar}}, from {{inh|es|la|praestāre}}, present active infinitive of {{m|la|praestō}}.

Coromines and Pascual mention an old attestation of Latin ''praestō'' meaning "to lend" in a legal document of 438, the ''Interpretationes Theodosianae'', where {{m|la|commodō}} is switched for ''praestō''. This meaning is also attested in the [[w:Reichenau Glosses|Reichenau Glosses]]. They also mention that the meaning "to borrow", generally considered non-standard, is already attested in the 16th-century work ''[[w:es:El patrañuelo|El patrañuelo]]''.

===Pronunciation===
{{es-IPA}}

===Verb===
{{es-verb}}

# {{lb|es|transitive}} to [[lend]]
#: {{ux|es|'''Presta'''me tu bicicleta.|'''Lend''' me your bicycle.}}
# {{lb|es|transitive}} to [[give]], [[pay]] {{gloss|e.g., attention}}
#: {{ux|es|¡'''Prestad''' atención, por favor!|'''Pay''' attention, please!}}
# {{lb|es|reflexive|transitive}} to have a natural inclination, a natural tendency
#: {{ux|es|El alcohol '''se presta''' al abuso.|Alcohol '''tends''' to be abused.}}
# {{lb|es|transitive}} to [[take]]
#: {{ux|es|Los ministros '''prestan''' el juramento.|The ministers '''take''' the oath.}}
# {{lb|es|transitive|nonstandard}} to [[borrow]]
#: {{ux|es|¿Le '''prestaste''' la laptop?|Did you '''borrow''' the laptop from her?}}
#: {{syn|es|pedir prestado|tomar prestado}}

====Conjugation====
{{es-conj}}

====Derived terms====
